--!strict
--[[
	IconAssets — GENERATED by tools/ui/icons/icons.py (sync). Do not edit by hand.

	Purpose:
		The rendered, 3D-looking UI icons (owner R9): HUD buttons, currencies, offers, rewards, game
		objects and the ten area icons. Each key maps to one uploaded Image asset (512 x 512, transparent,
		glossy shading, thick dark outline). An empty `image` means "not uploaded yet" or "moderation
		rejected it": UI/Kit/StudUI then draws its frame-built Glyphs fallback instead.

	Sources / licence:
		Most icons are Microsoft Fluent Emoji 3D (github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji), MIT License,
		Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation; outline, colour lift and composites by SellNukes. The rest
		are original Blender renders (tools/blender/ui_icons/render_icons.py). Full licence text and
		per-icon sources: assets/icons/LICENSE.md + assets/icons/sources.json; runbook: docs/icons.md.

	API:
		IconAssets.get(key)        -> IconEntry { image, size, category, source } (blank entry if unknown)
		IconAssets.image(key)      -> "rbxassetid://N" or nil (legacy helper used by StudUI / Toasts)
		IconAssets.Icons[key]      -> IconEntry       IconAssets.Ids[key] -> asset id (0 = none)
		IconAssets.Aliases[name]   -> key (legacy keys, MonetizationConfig product keys + icon names)
		IconAssets.Categories[cat] -> ordered keys (hud, currency, offer, reward, game, area, ui, event, world)
	Lookup order: exact key, exact alias, then case-insensitive (IconAssets.Lower), e.g. "SHOP".

	Example:
		local entry = IconAssets.get("Shop") -- also IconAssets.get("crown") -> the VIP icon
		imageLabel.Image = entry.image -- "" until uploaded: show the fallback glyph then
]]

